! Overview

''HyperGSD'' is a series of plugins that helps you <dfn>Get Stuff Done</dfn>, supported by a rich <dfn>Hypermedia</dfn> data model and associated tooling, to help you manage and prioritise the things you need to do.

HyperGSD carefully follows TiddlyWiki standards and uses the core's affordances as much as possible. It is intended to integrate with an all-in-one personal wiki, but you can also use it standalone. It is intended for use and tested against the vanilla theme, supporting.


; Actions (tasks)
: Short, single-step actions that accomplish a task.<br>Actions may also carry dependencies to/from other actions.
; Projects
: A collection of Actions that have a similar purpose or goal.
; Realms
: Divide your Actions/Projects into appropriate, custom groupings by tagging with <<tag-pill "$:/GSD/Realm/<RealmName>">> (e.g. <<tag-pill $:/GSD/Realm/Personal>>, <<tag-pill $:/GSD/Realm/Professional>>...)
; Dashboards for task management
: Manage your actions and projects through a number of dashboards.


! Install HyperGSD

Just drag-and-drop the main HyperGSD plugin to your wiki to install:

